<div style=3D"font-family: Verdana;font-size: 10.0pt;">
 <span style=3D"font-size: 10.0pt;">Dear Harry,</span></div>
 <div style=3D"font-family: Verdana;font-size: 10.0pt;"> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>I
 hope this email finds you well.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>I write to you today
 in relation to your Subject Access Request (SAR) &nbsp;recently submitted
 to the University.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>As outlined in the
 acknowledgement letter sent to you on 02 December 2025, the date by
 which we are required to respond to you is 30 December 2025. It is
 with regret that I inform you there will be a slight delay in
 providing you with the full set of documentation that you are
 entitled to under the right of access, meaning we will be unable to
 provide you with a response to your SAR by the 30 December deadline.
 I outline the reason for the delay below.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>The
 Information Governance Team has recently been experiencing
 significant resource constraints due to increased statutory
 workload, which in addition to the winter closure period (19/12/2025
 - 05/01/2026), means we require more time to process the remainder
 of your request.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>I recognise that this may not be
 the response you anticipated, however please be assured I hope to
 have the documentation that you are entitled to under the right of
 access without undue delay and would like to apologise for any
 inconvenience caused.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Please be assured, we are
 prioritising your request and will respond as soon as we are able to
 when the University re-opens in January.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Thank you
 for your patience and understanding.&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Kind
 regards,</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>James</p> </div>
